Time Complexity:
O(n)

Space Complexity:
O(1)

Approach:
1. Initialize curr = 0 to track the position of the last unique element
2. Traverse the array from index 1
3. Compare the current element with nums[curr]
4. If they are different, increment curr
5. Place the new unique element at index curr
6. Continue until the end of the array
7. Return curr + 1 as the count of unique elements



class Solution {
    public int removeDuplicates(int[] nums) {
        int curr = 0;
        for(int i=1; i<nums.length; i++){
            if(nums[curr] != nums[i]){
                curr++;
                int temp = nums[curr];
                nums[curr] = nums[i];
                nums[i] = temp;
            }
        }
        return curr+1;
    }
}
